  "title": "Flexible, Scalable, High Channel Count Stereo-Electrode for Recording in the Human Brain",
  "description": "This dataset contains intracranial EEG (iEEG) recordings acquired using novel flexible, scalable, high-channel-count micro-stereo-electrodes for direct neural recording in the human brain and animal models. The dataset includes raw and preprocessed (epoched) iEEG data collected across multiple species (humans, rodents, pigs, and non-human primates) to validate the performance and utility of the electrode technology. Direct electrical stimulation was employed to examine neural responses and characterize electrode functionality for high-resolution brain activity monitoring.",
  "methods_description": "Intracranial EEG data were recorded using flexible, scalable, high-channel-count stereo-electrodes. The dataset includes raw and preprocessed (epoched) recordings with binary files and channel maps provided in the derivatives folder. Direct electrical stimulation was used to examine effects of stimulation in the brain.",
